      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Given that the tangent line approximation to the function $f(x)$ at $x=1$ overestimates the values of the function in the neighborhood of $x=1,$ which of the following must be true?",
      "worked_solution": "Since the tangent line approximation of $f(x)$ at $x=1$ overestimates the values of the function, we have\n\n$$\nL(x)>f(x),\n$$\n\nthat is, the line $L(x)$ must be above the graph of $f(x)$ near the point  $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the function must be concave down in the neighborhood of $x=1.$",
